  "knowledge": "The framework rolls the transaction back, and PostgreSQL confirms the ROLLBACK, so the client knows that nothing committed.",
  "api_outcome": {
    "reported": "rolled_back",
    "basis": "the body threw and Connection.rollback() returned",
    "contract": "The unsafe jdbc-control policy reports committed whenever Connection.commit() returns, whatever PgConnection.getTransactionState() was before the call. It reports rolled_back when Connection.commit() throws. It calls Connection.commit() after Connection.rollback(Savepoint) has thrown. When Connection.rollback() throws, it calls Connection.setAutoCommit(true) and keeps the connection. Java 21 Connection.setAutoCommit says: \"If this method is called during a transaction and the auto-commit mode is changed, the transaction is committed.\" pgjdbc 42.7.14 PgConnection.setAutoCommit(true) calls commit() when auto-commit is off. It does not call Connection.setTransactionIsolation. A write made before a nested savepoint is executed inside that savepoint.",
    "error": {
      "class": "AppException",
      "code": null,
      "message": "application error: the request fails"
    },
    "steps": {}
  },
